  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Swiss city guide",
    "overview": "The confirmed direction is a light Swiss city guide: Helvetica typography, clear grids, flat structural regions, thin rules, and one signal-red accent. The existing rat-on-bridge mark is the single handmade detail. The signature interaction is exploring grouped venue markers, opening event detail, then planning a visit.\n\nThis refresh preserves the established direction contract. The tool route remains the starting kit, with its dark palette, rounded controls, and display-font suggestions explicitly overridden. Precedence is explicit user request, this file, taste/SIGNATURE.md, then Impeccable defaults. Product context is limited to the README and current routes: SF Rats supports local discovery and sharing, while the current application foregrounds Bay Area events. PRODUCT.md is absent; no additional audience or brand preferences are assumed. Amy rejected the dense grayscale map. Use authored vector cartography with blue water, green parks, golden main roads, sparse neighborhood labels, white venue markers and clickable event-count clusters. Reserve filled red for selected venues. Amy subsequently rejected the washed-out palette and oversized title: keep visible geographic color. Amy subsequently removed the explore heading entirely; do not restore it.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Helvetica throughout the interface.",
      "Near-white canvas, white surfaces, dark ink, and signal red.",
      "Flat event rows and compact filters organized by rules and alignment.",
      "Grouped venue markers and a distinct blue user-location indicator."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Signal Rule",
        "body": "Use the red accent to make actions, selected state, and event locations legible. The blue location indicator retains a separate meaning.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Structure Rule",
        "body": "Use alignment, tonal surfaces, and rules for the page structure. Soft shadows belong to floating overlays and map markers.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep the existing rat-on-bridge mark as the single handmade detail.",
      "Do use red for event markers, primary actions, and selected state; reserve blue for user location.",
      "Do preserve visible keyboard focus, stable control geometry, and reduced-motion interactions.",
      "Do keep date, type, nearby, and search filters in the unified toolbar.",
      "Do verify the map, dropdowns, and stacked event list at 390px without horizontal overflow."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't reintroduce paper grain, slanted stamps, decorative serif type, monospace interface labels, emoji icons, or hard offset shadows.",
      "Don't turn flat list rows into a grid of elevated cards.",
      "Don't fabricate event data or change persistent records as part of visual work.",
      "Don't treat legacy tracked uppercase labels in secondary controls as a new visual direction."
    ]
  }
